        <p>Illustrative proposals throughout the scenarios, notes and deep dives below: timings and caps are test inputs, not observed results or verified capabilities of either supplier. Model contribution as AOV × (margin − discount), with unchanged product cost; discount loss is AOV × discount. These figures exclude additional shipping, payment, messaging and return costs. Before every queued action, check current purchase, refund, stock and suppression state and permission for that channel and marketing purpose. Assign one queue owner, pause overlapping flows, and deduplicate replayed events by cart, customer and action; test those checks before enabling any channel.</p>
        <p>ActiveCampaign vs Sendlane: scenario 1 — B2B cart below MOQ threshold. At $44 AOV and 32% margin, full-price recovery contributes $14.08 vs $9.24 after a 11% code (Δ $4.84). Ladder touch 1 favors no-discount assist; watch for discount on email one before trust proof. Email 1 ~59m, email 2 ~23h, SMS branch ~7h for opted-in only.</p>
        <p>ActiveCampaign vs Sendlane: scenario 2 — logged-in repeat buyer with saved address. At $44 AOV and 32% margin, full-price recovery contributes $14.08 vs $9.24 after a 11% code (Δ $4.84). Ladder touch 2 favors email proof; watch for SMS after 9pm local without quiet hours. Email 1 ~59m, email 2 ~23h, SMS branch ~7h for opted-in only.</p>
        <p>ActiveCampaign vs Sendlane: scenario 3 — international shipping quote sticker shock. At $44 AOV and 32% margin, full-price recovery contributes $14.08 vs $9.24 after a 11% code (Δ $4.84). Ladder touch 3 favors SMS urgency; watch for no suppression after partial refund. Email 1 ~59m, email 2 ~23h, SMS branch ~7h for opted-in only.</p>
        <p>ActiveCampaign vs Sendlane: scenario 4 — subscription toggle left on at checkout. At $44 AOV and 32% margin, full-price recovery contributes $14.08 vs $9.24 after a 11% code (Δ $4.84). Ladder touch 4 favors push nudge; watch for attribution credit on would-have-returned orders. Email 1 ~59m, email 2 ~23h, SMS branch ~7h for opted-in only.</p>
        <p>ActiveCampaign vs Sendlane: scenario 5 — first-time mobile shopper on Instagram traffic. At $44 AOV and 32% margin, full-price recovery contributes $14.08 vs $9.24 after a 11% code (Δ $4.84). Ladder touch 1 favors no-discount assist; watch for recovery for fully OOS cart. Email 1 ~59m, email 2 ~23h, SMS branch ~7h for opted-in only.</p>
        <p>ActiveCampaign vs Sendlane: scenario 6 — size matrix with two variants OOS. At $44 AOV and 32% margin, full-price recovery contributes $14.08 vs $9.24 after a 11% code (Δ $4.84). Ladder touch 2 favors email proof; watch for duplicate SMS and email within 20 minutes. Email 1 ~59m, email 2 ~23h, SMS branch ~7h for opted-in only.</p>
